== (1) the 1:2 split: Z[w] (n <= 20000) and the Hurwitz order (n <= 400)
  Z[w]: r(n) = 6 sum chi_-3 for all n <= 20000: True; odd n: first = 2 sum chi_-3 = r/3, centred = 2 first: True; even n: centred = 0: True
  Hurwitz, n <= 400: odd n: Lipschitz 8 sigma(n), centred 16 sigma(n); even n: Lipschitz 24 sigma(odd part), centred 0: True
  units of order 3: N(w - 1) = 3 and N(zeta - 1) = 3 (odd), so both act on F4* by a 3-cycle
