== (3) the cubic character of 2 (all p = 1 mod 3 below 10^6)
  39231 primes; mismatches of (b even) <=> (2 cubic residue) <=> (p = x^2 + 27y^2): 0; 2 a cubic residue for 13032 (0.3322); the symbol (2/pi)_3 equals pi mod 2 in {1, w, w^2} for every p: True; the conjugate primary prime has the same grid: True
  p < 50: 7: pi = 2+3w (centred), 13: pi = -4-3w (centred), 19: pi = 2-3w (centred), 31: pi = -1-6w (first), 37: pi = -4+3w (centred), 43: pi = -7-6w (first)
  Mersenne: the listed x^2 + 27y^2 representations of 2^q - 1 (q = 5..127) are correct, 2 is a cube via 3m = 1 (mod q), and (q <= 61) the primary prime recomputed by a Euclidean gcd gives the same (x, y): True; q = 3 excluded
== (4) designs and identities
  {+-1}                           : design strength 1 (moment test) / 1 (Gegenbauer test); 2-design False, 4-design False, 6-design False
  {+-w, +-w^2}                    : design strength 1 (moment test) / 1 (Gegenbauer test); 2-design False, 4-design False, 6-design False
  hexagon                         : design strength 5 (moment test) / 5 (Gegenbauer test); 2-design True, 4-design True, 6-design False
  16-cell                         : design strength 3 (moment test) / 3 (Gegenbauer test); 2-design True, 4-design False, 6-design False
  tesseract                       : design strength 3 (moment test) / 3 (Gegenbauer test); 2-design True, 4-design False, 6-design False
  24-cell                         : design strength 5 (moment test) / 5 (Gegenbauer test); 2-design True, 4-design True, 6-design False
  square                          : design strength 3 (moment test) / 3 (Gegenbauer test); 2-design True, 4-design False, 6-design False
  octagon (d = 1 two-grid units)  : design strength 7 (moment test) / 7 (Gegenbauer test); 2-design True, 4-design True, 6-design True
  Candido: True; Liouville: True; sum over hexagon <u,x>^4 = (9/4)|x|^4: True; sum over 24-cell = 3|x|^4: True; octagon identity 6(a^2+b^2)^2 = 4a^4 + 4b^4 + (a+b)^4 + (a-b)^4: True
  (1+i) * Hurwitz units = the 24 roots of D4 (left: True, right: True)
  negative controls: Candido with 3 instead of 2: False; Liouville with 5 instead of 6: False; 24-cell minus one point has design strength 0
== (5) Eisenstein fourth powers mod 16, (6) sums of four
  fourth powers mod 16: [(0, 0), (0, 1), (0, 9), (1, 0), (7, 7), (9, 0), (15, 15)]
  alpha in 2Z[w] -> 0; else u or 9u with u = alpha^4 mod 2: True; mu6^4 = [(-1, -1), (0, 1), (1, 0)] = {1, w, w^2}
  rational residues mod 16 of four fourth powers: over Z [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]; over the first grid Z[sqrt-3] [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 9, 10, 11, 12]; over Z[w] [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 14, 15]
  negative control: adding the false residue 5 to the fourth-power set makes [5, 13] reachable
FAILURES: 0
